{"id":"rehum","name":"Rehum","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:rehum"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Rehum","text":"Merciful. (1.) One of “the children of the province” who returned from the Captivity (Ezra 2:2); the same as “Nehum” (Neh. 7:7). (2.) The “chancellor” of Artaxerxes, who sought to stir him up against the Jews (Ezra 4:8-24) and prevent the rebuilding of the walls and the temple of Jerusalem. (3.) A Levite (Neh. 3:17). (4.) Neh. 10:25. (5.) A priest (Neh. 12:3)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H7348","lemma":"רְחוּם","xlit":"Rᵉchûwm","gloss":"Rechum, the name of a Persian and of three Israelites","kjv":"Rehum","count":8,"share":0.89},{"strong":"H8124","lemma":"שִׁמְשַׁי","xlit":"Shimshay","gloss":"Shimshai, a Samaritan","kjv":"Shimshai","count":4,"share":0.44},{"strong":"H5613","lemma":"סָפֵר","xlit":"çâphêr","gloss":"a scribe","kjv":"scribe","count":4,"share":0.44},{"strong":"H1169","lemma":"בְּעֵל","xlit":"bᵉʻêl","gloss":"{a master","kjv":"chancellor","count":3,"share":0.33},{"strong":"H3675","lemma":"כְּנָת","xlit":"kᵉnâth","gloss":"{a colleague }","kjv":"companion","count":3,"share":0.33},{"strong":"H1114","lemma":"בִּלְשָׁן","xlit":"Bilshân","gloss":"Bilshan, an Israelite","kjv":"Bilshan","count":2,"share":0.22}],"verses":["Ezra.2.2","Ezra.4.8","Ezra.4.9","Ezra.4.17","Ezra.4.23","Neh.3.17","Neh.10.25","Neh.12.3","Neh.7.7"],"related":[{"id":"shimshai","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.444,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"chancellor","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.333,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"bishlam","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.174,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"artaxerxes","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.154,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"nehemiah","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.057,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"persia","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.027,"why":"5 verses are